new file mode 100644
index 0000000..653ee35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/mojo-runtime.md
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# Baking the Mojo runtime into the SLC
+
+A Mojo UDF ships as a `mojo build --emit shared-lib` shared object that the host
+`dlopen`s at query time. That `.so` links against the **Mojo runtime libraries**
+(stdlib + codegen runtime). The SLC is a *hermetic root filesystem* — it contains
+only a documented library surface, no package manager — so those runtime `.so`s
+must be staged into the image, or every Mojo UDF dies at load with an
+undefined-symbol / missing-library error.
+
+The container never compiles user UDFs (authors build the `.so` themselves, like
+Rust UDFs built with `cargo exasol-udf build`), so only the **runtime** is needed
+here, not the Mojo compiler.
+
+## Building the image with the Mojo runtime
+
+Off by default. Enable it at build time:
+
+```bash
+# via the installer
+scripts/install.sh --with-mojo --host … --password … --bfs-password …
+# pin the toolchain version (recommended)
+MOJO_VERSION=25.6 scripts/install.sh --with-mojo …
+
+# or directly
+docker build -f Dockerfile --target artifact \
+  --build-arg WITH_MOJO=1 --build-arg MOJO_VERSION=25.6 \
+  --output type=local,dest=./out .
+```
+
+`WITH_MOJO=0` (the default) leaves the `mojo-runtime` donor stage empty, so the
+staging copy is a no-op and the image is byte-for-byte the Rust-only SLC.
+
+## ⚠️ What must be verified
+
+The `mojo-runtime` stage in the `Dockerfile` is **not verified** — it was authored
+without a Mojo toolchain available. Before relying on it, confirm two things
+against the actual Mojo release you target:
+
+1. **Install channel.** The stage uses `pip install modular==$MOJO_VERSION`. If
+   your toolchain ships via `pixi`/`magic` or a different package, replace that
+   line.
+2. **Runtime library surface.** The stage currently copies *every* `*.so*` under
+   the installed `modular` package. That is a safe superset but larger than
+   necessary. Determine the true surface from a real UDF:
+
+   ```bash
+   mojo build --emit shared-lib examples/double.mojo -o libdouble.so
+   ldd libdouble.so
+   ```
+
+   Every line that is **not** a base-glibc library already staged by the SLC
+   (libc, libm, libpthread, libdl, libgcc_s, ld-linux…) is a Mojo runtime lib you
+   must stage. Record those sonames — this is the Mojo analogue of
+   `crates/cargo-exasol-udf/slc-library-surface.txt`.
+
+3. **glibc floor.** The Mojo runtime must not require a newer glibc than the SLC's
+   base (`crates/cargo-exasol-udf/slc-glibc-floor.txt`). Check with
+   `objdump -T libMojo*.so* | grep GLIBC_` and compare against the floor.
+
+## Fingerprint agreement
+
+The Mojo SDK stamps the vtable `fingerprint` as `mojo:<sdk_version>`, which the
+host accepts via the `mojo-bridge` fingerprint relaxation
+(`crates/exa-udf-runtime/src/loader.rs`). Keep `MOJO_VERSION` (the runtime baked
+into the image) and the SDK version that stamps the fingerprint on the same
+toolchain release, so the runtime the `.so` links matches the one in the image.
